uling, IO and low-level architecture.\nK-SIM Simulation domains: physics, destruction, fluids, cloth, crowds, large-scale simulation, determinism of simulation.\nK-NET Online and multiplayer architecture: models, replication, prediction, servers, security, online-service boundaries.\nK-TOOLS Production tooling and content workflows: editor, pipeline, collaboration, iteration speed.\nK-PLATFORM Hardware, operating systems, consoles, graphics APIs, packaging and platform requirements.\nK-PERF Scalability bottlenecks: serialization points, excess synchronization, cache inefficiency, GPU stalls, bandwidth, poor asymptotics.\nK-PROD Could a real team ship games with this: workflows, content scale, team scale, schedules, live operations.\nK-FUTURE Does the architecture block likely next-5-year technologies: neural rendering, work graphs, cluster RT, ML animation, new storage and memory, new plat\nK-COMPLETE Exactly one responsibility: find engine capabilities or engineering disciplines that are missing.\nK-LEGACY Find accidental legacy architecture: central sequential update loops, deep inheritance, global state, hot-path virtual dispatch, CPU-driven rendering,\nK-GAMEPLAY Animation, audio, AI, gameplay framework, UI, text, localization and accessibility: whether game teams get what they need.\nK-TEST Validation, oracles, determinism and concurrency testing, agent-output integrity: can an independent critic objectively decide correctness?\nK-SEC Threat model, trust boundaries, memory safety, supply chain, privacy, incident response — reviewed at design time as well as in code.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"492b321c-e7db-4810-95c2-f1ad55bf9459","timestamp":"2026-09-30T08:03:22.019Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"75331139-532d-44bc-aef9-4606bb4c3880","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan